@startuml

' =============================================================
' UC-005 Phone List Coordination - Use Case Diagram (PIM)
'
' MDA Level: Platform Independent Model
' Perspective: Specification / Analysis
'
' Derived from CIM use case overview by applying mapping rules
' M1 (Business Actor -> System Actor) and M2 (Business Goal ->
' System Use Case) and M4 (Implicit Knowledge -> Explicit Behavior).
'
' Compare with: ../../cim/uc-005-dashBoard-phoneList/uc-005.usecase-overview.cim.puml
'
' Differences from CIM:
' - "Caregiver on Shift" becomes "Caregiver" (system role)
' - New actor: System Time Event (introduced by M1)
' - Business goals become system interactions
' - <<include>> shows shared validation behavior
' - Still NO technology, NO UI, NO platform
' =============================================================

title UC-005 Phone List Coordination — Use Case Diagram (PIM)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam usecaseBackgroundColor #E6F4FF
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #FFF4E6
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

' --- System actors (PIM-level: roles, not real persons) ---
actor "Caregiver" as Caregiver
actor "Shift Coordinator" as Coordinator
actor "System Time Event" as TimeEvent <<system>>

' --- System boundary ---
package "Phone Coordination System" <<System>> #F0F0F0 {

    usecase "View phone list\nfor active shift" as UC_View
    usecase "Assign caregiver name\nto phone" as UC_Assign
    usecase "Clear assignment" as UC_Clear
    usecase "Refresh phone list\nautomatically" as UC_Refresh
    usecase "Validate assignment\nagainst business rules" as UC_Validate

}

' --- Actor-to-use-case associations ---
Caregiver --> UC_View
Caregiver --> UC_Assign
Caregiver --> UC_Clear
Coordinator --> UC_View
TimeEvent --> UC_Refresh

' --- Use case relationships ---
UC_Assign ..> UC_Validate : <<include>>
UC_Clear ..> UC_Validate : <<include>>
UC_Refresh ..> UC_View : <<include>>

note bottom of "Phone Coordination System"
    <b>Transformation from CIM:</b>
    Rule M1: "Caregiver on Shift" -> "Caregiver" (system role)
    Rule M1: New actor "System Time Event" introduced
    Rule M2: Business goals mapped to system interactions
    Rule M4: Implicit validation made explicit as separate use case

    <b>Still NOT included (PSM concerns):</b>
    - No UI elements (no "click", "form", "screen")
    - No technology (no .NET, no REST, no database)
    - No persistence strategy
    - No specific data types

    <b>Note on "System Time Event":</b>
    This actor exists ONLY at PIM/PSM level. It represents
    the system's internal capability to react to time passing.
    In CIM there is no such actor — automatic refresh is a
    system concern, not a business concern.
end note

@enduml
